---
source: crates/ambers-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: "ok_stdout(&[\"view\", \"--help\"])"
---
Browse a file's data in a full-screen grid

Like SPSS's Data View: move with the arrow keys, press Tab to switch between value labels, stored codes and both, Enter for one respondent's answers, i for the variable list, ? for every key. Needs an interactive terminal.

Usage: ambers view [OPTIONS] <FILE>

Arguments:
  <FILE>
          Path to a .sav or .zsav file

Options:
      --mode <MODE>
          What cells show at the start; Tab cycles through all three

          Possible values:
          - labels: The value label, or the value itself when it has none
          - codes:  The stored value
          - both:   The stored value followed by its label
          
          [default: labels]

      --limit <N>
          Load at most N rows (the rest of a larger file is not read)
          
          [default: 1000000]

      --theme <THEME>
          Colours

          Possible values:
          - dracula:  The Dracula palette, the same in every terminal
          - terminal: Your terminal's own colours
          
          [default: dracula]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
